  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Strengthening National Response and Reintegration Mechanisms for migrant returnees in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The proposed intervention seeks to enhance Ethiopia&apos;s support for vulnerable migrants, particularly returnees, by strengthening the national referral mechanism and providing comprehensive services at both individual and community levels in a complementary way to other interventions targeting return and reintegration. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt;State and non-state actors will be empowered to gradually provide these services directly.&lt;/span&gt; The project focuses on sustainable reintegration through livelihood support, health and psychosocial services, and community-driven initiatives. The project puts a strong emphasis on strengthening the capacity of Ethiopian government agencies and local stakeholders to manage migration, in particular reintegration assistance, improving Ethiopia&apos;s migration governance framework. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt; Finally, the action will empower youth on migration-related decision through the use of innovative ways of engagement, leveraging and equipping local state and non-state actors to carry on such efforts over time. Ultimately, this action will allow to gradually transition away from individual reintegration packages provided via &lt;/span&gt;implementing&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt; partners towards a sustainable, inclusive and effective national-owned referral system for reintegration. During this transition, due attention will be paid to ensuring there is no duplication of services or overlap between the support provided under this action and the support provided under other programmes. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
